From a32e61001ec8fb6eface53202e30fdfaf775b8a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:23:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/42] Recover the exec security configuration functions

Replace the remaining stubs in kern_exec_security.c with bodies recovered
from the reference kernel image: the hardened-browser entitlement block,
the platform-binary task flag, IPC containment and WebKit signing-id
detection, the IPC security policy hook, and the VFS resolve-flags
entitlement parse.

The reference carries an exec_security_state byte in load_result_t and
tracks it through kern_exec_security.h.  Add the related task security
config bits (vm_containment_vessel_cow_defeatured, reserved2, webkit),
the proc and proc_ro VFS resolve flag fields with their accessors, and
move the shared EXEC_LOG and platform-restriction entitlement macros into
kern_exec_internal.h.

The hardened-browser GPU and network entitlement strings in the reference
image read ...gpu and ...network, differing from the matching KDK's
CodeSignature/Entitlements.h; the recovered source carries its own
definitions.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
